WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.800
Now look, here's the thing.

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:05.980
Last week, we did our first
Clueless Gamer in two years!

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:07.020
Whoa!
Yeah!

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:09.577
Not dog years, two human years.

00:00:09.577 --> 00:00:10.860
(Sonja laughs)

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:12.940
Two years, it's mind-blowing.

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:13.773
Wild.

00:00:13.773 --> 00:00:16.300
It was really weird and wild and fun.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:17.280
It was really fun.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:21.290
The game was "Biomutant,"
the celebrity was JB Smoove,

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:24.880
and it's so funny because,
like Sonja, you know,

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:28.850
we have been doing this
podcast now for quite a while.

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:30.620
But we haven't

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:32.360
done one since

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:33.450
we haven't done a Clueless Gamer

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:34.920
since we started this podcast

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:36.290
which is crazy to think about
(Sonja) Whoa!

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:37.123
Isn't that weird?

00:00:37.123 --> 00:00:39.290
That is crazy to think about. (laughs)

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:40.320
(Aaron) And like.
Oh my gosh.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:42.830
We did it at Largo in person

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:46.210
but I haven't seen Conan
in person for a year.

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:47.140
Oh my God.

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:49.590
But you know, we did
"Biomutant," which was the game

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:51.290
is super fun.

00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:55.890
And you know, I mean, Clueless
Gamer, it's a comedy bit

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:59.417
you know. So I played, they
gave me the game beforehand,

00:00:59.417 --> 00:01:02.740
and so, you know, I go through
with two of our writers,

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:04.620
Levi and Glenn, and we
wrote a bunch of jokes

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:07.350
and areas and stuff that
would be good for Conan.

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:09.710
And this was the kind
of perfect game because,

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:12.510
you know, it's easy to play
for him, which is good.

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:14.593
So he could actually
fight, which is great.

00:01:14.593 --> 00:01:16.070
That is a huge achievement.

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:17.195
Huge achievement.

00:01:17.195 --> 00:01:18.900
The world is great.

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:22.030
It's full of all these
like mutated animals

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:24.080
which is beautiful comedy gold, you know,

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:25.860
for like a comedy bit, it's perfect.

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:28.200
It's... it looks insane.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:31.110
It looks great. It's gorgeous,
but it's a wild world.

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:32.720
It's so hard, you know,
when you do something

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:35.750
like a Call of Duty or
you do something like a,

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:37.580
you know, when we did Tomb Raider.

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:39.570
It's hard when it's like human beings

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:40.820
Right.
To make comedy

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:43.010
out of that, and we've done
so many of these comedy bits

00:01:43.010 --> 00:01:43.843
that like.
But when

00:01:43.843 --> 00:01:45.220
they're mutant animals.

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:47.040
Well, yeah, which is great.
A little more to pull from.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.170
Yeah!
Any favorites?

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:50.490
Absolutely. I mean I think that.

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:53.940
And the great thing is
there was this moment where,

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:56.420
so there were these four
World Eaters in the game,

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:58.630
and they're these basically
they're giant boss fights.

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:02.180
And so we did a thing,
which is the Jumbo Puff

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:04.810
which is the first World
Eater you kinda come across.

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:07.740
Then we had them fight, and
as I was playing Jumbo Puff

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:09.430
for the first time,

00:02:09.430 --> 00:02:12.530
it's great because you're
in this giant mech suit.

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:15.700
So that's great. A lot of
explosions and fun action,

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:16.533
which is great.

00:02:16.533 --> 00:02:17.530
Very cool.
But then,

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:19.810
the, you know, there's
three kind of phases

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:21.460
to this boss battle.

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:24.270
And the third one is he eats you,

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:26.550
and you go down inside of him.

00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:27.540
Oh my God.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:30.200
And if you don't swim immediately to like

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:33.330
the esophagus wall, he poops you out.

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:34.820
Which is hilarious, you know,

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:36.920
And then he sits on you
and it's like, hilarious.

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:40.210
So right away, I knew we had
a great ender for the bit,

00:02:40.210 --> 00:02:41.043
you know?
(Sonja laughs)

00:02:41.043 --> 00:02:41.876
Ender?
'Cause that's the thing.

00:02:41.876 --> 00:02:42.997
Well, it's (laughs) good one.

00:02:42.997 --> 00:02:43.990
(Sonja laughs)

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:45.480
But that's always kind
of the thing, is like,

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:48.520
how do we get that? How
do we get the temperature

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:50.770
to a boiling point for the actual game?

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:53.160
So the, the comedy piece
has a good, good ending.

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:55.120
So I knew when I played
the Jumbo Puff, we were,

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:55.953
we were in good hands.

00:02:55.953 --> 00:02:57.490
But.
I was gonna say that,

00:02:57.490 --> 00:03:01.430
Jumbo Puff sounds delicious
but then everything

00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:03.517
that you just said changed my mind.

00:03:03.517 --> 00:03:05.258
(Aaron and Sonja laugh)

00:03:05.258 --> 00:03:08.100
But it was great and JB Smoove,

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:11.330
aside from being just one
of the funniest people alive

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:14.730
and an amazing improviser,
also like, you know,

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:16.840
the great thing about
him is he plays games.

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:19.140
He's been in "Grand Theft
Auto," and he's actually.

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:21.760
So like these other
Clueless Gamers we've done

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:24.700
with like people like
Kumail or Ron Funches

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:26.590
who actually play games.

00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:28.570
It just, it's so much easier

00:03:28.570 --> 00:03:30.120
because he's just doing the things.

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:31.930
So it's not me being like, okay, go left.

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:32.763
Okay, do this.

00:03:32.763 --> 00:03:33.730
(Sonja hums in agreement)
So that.

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:35.610
That, so JB was a real treat as well.

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:38.100
So we asked you guys to
send a few questions in

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:42.420
about the last Clueless Gamer,
and we've got a bunch here.

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:43.950
You ready?
Let's do it.

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:44.783
Alright.

00:03:44.783 --> 00:03:46.860
So ChavChihiro,

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:48.910
I'm so sorry if I butchered that

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:52.050
but they asked, did clone,
did Clonan? (laughs)

00:03:52.050 --> 00:03:52.883
Clonan?
(Sonja laughs)

00:03:52.883 --> 00:03:55.850
That's Conan's clone, for
people who don't know.

00:03:55.850 --> 00:03:58.396
Did Conan have much of a say
in the character creation

00:03:58.396 --> 00:04:01.910
in the last Clueless
Gamer or was that all JB?

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:04.840
Well, it's interesting,
like again, I think like,

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:07.420
you know, we're making
like a piece of comedy

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:09.840
and to make that piece
of comedy I need to play

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:11.370
a lot of the game.

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:14.720
So I had to get far in the
game with a certain character.

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:16.440
So here's kind of a dirty secret just

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:18.580
for our podcast listeners.

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:21.510
They had fun talking about
the character creator,

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:24.430
which is, in "Biomutant,"
very robust and very fun,

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:26.530
but they had to pick the character

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:28.780
that I originally created.
(Sonja gasps)

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:30.720
So it matched later.

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:31.553
So it matched.
Uh-huh

00:04:31.553 --> 00:04:34.600
So the footage matches. We
did that in "Skyrim" too.

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:36.830
I personally had played a Khajiit

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:38.390
who's like a cat.

00:04:38.390 --> 00:04:39.860
Cat race.

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:41.170
In "Skyrim."

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:44.070
So when we were doing the
character creator part

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:46.810
in "Skyrim" as well. Jokes, jokes, jokes,

00:04:46.810 --> 00:04:49.780
but then he needs to land
on a certain character.

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:52.910
So you're the man behind
the character creation.

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:53.743
The boy
In all.

00:04:53.743 --> 00:04:54.993
I'm really a boy. I'm not really a man.

00:04:54.993 --> 00:04:57.370
(laughs) You are the bouncing baby boy -

00:04:57.370 --> 00:04:58.405
behind

00:04:58.405 --> 00:04:59.750
the character creation.

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:03.350
Yeah. So they did their,
they do all their comedy

00:05:03.350 --> 00:05:06.233
but then I did have to have them land on,

00:05:06.233 --> 00:05:09.760
I think it was the Hyla character
'cause it was the toughest

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:11.360
because I knew Conan
would get beat up a lot.

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:12.782
So I chose that race.
(Sonja laughs)

00:05:12.782 --> 00:05:14.460
That mutant.

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:16.700
I love these, I love
the behind the scenes.

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:17.976
Yeah. There we go.
I love the behind the scenes

00:05:17.976 --> 00:05:20.310
Nolan Y. wants to know

00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:24.003
are there any games that Conan
was surprisingly adept at?

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:26.475
No. Next question.

00:05:26.475 --> 00:05:29.070
(Sonja laughs)

00:05:29.070 --> 00:05:29.930
Not one?

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:31.540
Not a single, no?

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:32.373
He's terrible.

00:05:32.373 --> 00:05:33.206
Oh, Okay. All right.

00:05:33.206 --> 00:05:35.080
Even when we did "ARMS" with Will Arnett

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:36.770
which is all motion tracking

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:38.450
of him punching, he's still terrible.

00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:39.520
It's, he can't do it.
(Sonja laughs)

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:40.750
It's, he's, you know?

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:41.583
Maybe one day.

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:45.720
Ashwin Shaji, again, I'm so
sorry if I butchered that,

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:49.050
but they would like to know favorite game

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:50.910
that Aaron has played with Conan.

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:53.386
I'm trying to think of the
one I got beat up the least.

00:05:53.386 --> 00:05:54.500
(Sonja laughs)

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:57.190
The one where you've
endured the least abuse.

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:59.490
There was one where he
smashed three chairs on me

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:00.863
in succession. So that would be the least

00:06:00.863 --> 00:06:02.500
favorite game.
That's your favorite. Oh.

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:05.140
No. I honestly, I think,
you know what I'll say?

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:08.120
The next one. I think like every,

00:06:08.120 --> 00:06:12.580
every Clueless Gamer has
is fun in its own way

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:16.260
and is tough in another way.

00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:18.380
But I think that.

00:06:18.380 --> 00:06:20.340
This one was great, 'cause JB was great

00:06:20.340 --> 00:06:22.800
and the game was fun, but.

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:23.960
But yeah, I think that's it.

00:06:23.960 --> 00:06:25.700
And this was, this was great.

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:27.860
And I have to say like,
in terms of shooting

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:30.470
like in terms of us actually filming this.

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:33.860
Like Conan and JB are so
great together and the fact

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:36.930
that "Biomutant," like the
combat, you could just,

00:06:36.930 --> 00:06:39.370
it's very kind of easy to pick up.

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:42.420
So that made it a fun
one to do with Conan.

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:44.580
Like people always want like,
oh, what about "Dark Souls?"

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:46.100
I'm like, it's just
gonna be Conan dying over

00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:47.220
and over and over.
(Sonja laughs)

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:48.870
How can we make something
funny out of that?

00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:50.427
But so this was, this was really great.

00:06:50.427 --> 00:06:51.730
I love that. So you have fun.

00:06:51.730 --> 00:06:53.460
You love, you're into "Biomutant."

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:55.490
It was really fun and I'm really happy

00:06:55.490 --> 00:06:57.610
Clueless Gamer's back and.

00:06:57.610 --> 00:07:00.420
Yeah, I'm excited to hopefully
get another one on the books.

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:02.430
Yes.
So I have a couple ideas

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:04.110
of ones that I think would be great

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:06.150
Ooh-lala
For another one

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:08.780
and if you guys have ideas, tweet at us

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:12.150
at @GoodGameNiceTry or
use the hashtag #GGNT

00:07:12.150 --> 00:07:15.100
of games you think that would
be fun for a Clueless Gamer.

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:16.550
Obviously, we all think

00:07:16.550 --> 00:07:18.358
"Resident Evil Village" would be fun.

00:07:18.358 --> 00:07:21.640
So yes, of course. I would
love to try to do that one,

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:24.210
but other games I might not
know about or hear about.

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:25.043
Let us know.

